                                "sense_id": "0a2dd34c-f89d-3576-8b37-3f4faef06168",
                                "text": "Piano technicians have to measurements at their disposal for measuring touchweight: downweight and upweight. Downweight and upweight are measured in grams. To measure downweight, a gram weight is placed on the key at the front and a rap or thump is given to the shop bench, KEYBED, or action stack with one's fist to break the starting friction"
                            }
                        ]
